From: mscharged-port
Subject: Build the Dawn platform without exceptions
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host build fix (every platform; the failure shows on macOS). Apply after 0117.

TracyPlatform.cpp implements Dawn's platform interfaces, so it is built
without RTTI, as Dawn is. Since 0105 it always holds the worker pool, whose
std::vector, std::deque and std::make_shared can throw. With RTTI off but
exceptions on, Clang emits the type info of every exception these can throw
(std::exception, logic_error, length_error, bad_alloc, bad_array_new_length)
into this object. On Apple arm64 they are hidden definitions, and the static
linker binds every reference in the program to them instead of the system's
libc++abi: catch (const std::exception&) then no longer matches a
std::runtime_error or std::filesystem::filesystem_error, whose type info
comes from the system, and such an exception ended the program instead.

Dawn builds its own sources with -fno-rtti -fno-exceptions; this file now
does too, and emits no type info. It neither throws nor catches.

diff --git a/cmake/aurora_core.cmake b/cmake/aurora_core.cmake
index 4534e60..e1b076d 100644
--- a/cmake/aurora_core.cmake
+++ b/cmake/aurora_core.cmake
@@ -96,7 +96,9 @@ if (AURORA_ENABLE_GX)
             lib/dawn/TracyPlatform.cpp
     )
     if (CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_FRONTEND_VARIANT STREQUAL "GNU")
-        set_source_files_properties(lib/dawn/TracyPlatform.cpp PROPERTIES COMPILE_FLAGS -fno-rtti)
+        # Like Dawn itself, also without exceptions: under -fno-rtti, Clang would give the program a hidden copy
+        # of std::exception's type info, and on macOS no catch (const std::exception&) would match the system's.
+        set_source_files_properties(lib/dawn/TracyPlatform.cpp PROPERTIES COMPILE_FLAGS "-fno-rtti -fno-exceptions")
     endif ()
     target_link_libraries(aurora_core PRIVATE dawn::webgpu_dawn)
     if (DAWN_ENABLE_VULKAN)
